**`src/bookmarks.ts`** — added `filterByTags`:

```ts
export function filterByTags(bookmarks: Bookmark[], tags: string[]): Bookmark[] {
  if (tags.length === 0) return bookmarks;
  return bookmarks.filter((b) => tags.every((t) => b.tags.includes(t)));
}
```

Behavior:
- Empty `tags` → returns all bookmarks (no filtering).
- Non-empty `tags` → AND semantics: a bookmark is included only if it has **every** tag in the array (uses `Array.prototype.every`).

